    <name>
      <text>Indefinite Integral of a Polynomial</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the indefinite integral:</p>
\[ \int \left( {@integrand@} \right) \, dx \]
<p><em>Use \(c\) for the constant of integration.</em></p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Apply the power rule for integration term by term:</p>
\[ \int x^k \, dx = \frac{x^{k+1}}{k+1} + c \quad (k \neq -1) \]
<p>For the given integrand:</p>
\[ \int \left( {@integrand@} \right) \, dx = {@a@} \cdot \frac{x^{{@n+1@}}}{{@n+1@}} + {@b@} \cdot \frac{x^2}{2} + c \]
\[ = {@ta1@} \]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>demo-power-integral</idnumber>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025102100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[/* Indefinite integral using the power rule */
a: rand([2, 3, 4, 5, 6]);
b: rand([2, 4, 6, 8]);
n: rand([2, 3, 4]);

integrand: a*x^n + b*x;
ta1: a*x^(n+1)/(n+1) + (b/2)*x^2 + c;

/* Common misconceptions */
ans_diff: diff(integrand, x);
ans_no_c: a*x^(n+1)/(n+1) + (b/2)*x^2;
]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
